        "answer": {
          "short": "Not identical: $x=1$ is excluded.\n\nSimplify only after finding the original domain.",
          "worked": "The logarithm requires $\\dfrac{x^2-1}{x-1}>0$, with $x\\ne1$. Factoring gives the domain $(-1,1)\\cup(1,\\infty)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\ln(x+1)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis agrees with the target expression on its domain, but the point $(1,\\ln2)$ is missing. The graphs are not identical.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
